## Blocking Issues
- **Wave 1, QA6 (fixed in `58aa50f`).** A total of 1,234,567.00 printed as `1234,567.00`. Fix row 1 rewrote `groupThousands` and added a regression test, which failed before the fix. `bun test` now shows 5 pass and 0 fail.
- **Delta review, first pass: REJECT.** It rejected carrying the s1 happy-path row without re-running it. I re-ran s1 on `58aa50f` (`25.00`, exit 0). A fresh review of the same range returned OKAY.
- **Wave 2, B1 `sub-cent-rounding` at `src/money.ts:2`.** A price like `1.005` rounds to 1.00. It is left unfixed: `gate.md`'s accepted residual risk names exactly this. It is recorded as one `downgrades` entry (rule `accepted-residual`, disposition `residual`) under `override.by: Tim`.

## Covered by one invocation
Correctness, architecture, wire contracts, security/privacy and verification were all covered by the single implementation-audit.

## Recommendations
- **No separate review worktree.** `feat/csv-total` is checked out in this checkout, the only worktree. Adding another worktree on the same branch would have needed `--force`, so the gate ran here.
- **Planning review is stale.** Adding fix row 1 to `tasks.md` changed the folder, so `validate-openspec-change.mjs --reviewed` now reports `review.md` as stale. It passed at `ecd418f`; the gate's own plan check passes.
- **One capture left untracked.** `wave-1/q6-regression-grouping.md`, the failing wave-1 capture, stays untracked because the record doesn't cite it.

